            <ArticleTitle>Gadolinium-based coronarography in a patient with renal failure: first clinical report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reports the use of gadolinium to perform a coronarography in a patient with renal insufficiency, unstable angina, and peripheral vascular disease. The examination was well tolerated and the images obtained of good quality. Cathet Cardiovasc Intervent 2001;54:68-69.</AbstractText>
